b=(0)+(1)r, ac=1: closed form == E[P^m] for m=1..10: True
b=(1)+(1)r, ac=1: closed form == E[P^m] for m=1..10: True
b=(2)+(1)r, ac=1: closed form == E[P^m] for m=1..10: True
b=(1)+(-1)r, ac=1: closed form == E[P^m] for m=1..10: True
b=(1)+(2)r, ac=3: closed form == E[P^m] for m=1..10: True

Nullcone condition, coefficient equations (symbolic by hand, verified):
  t^1: b0 = -b1
  t^2: g  = -b1^2/2
  t^3: g*b1 = -b1^3/3  =>  g = -b1^2/3   (if b1!=0)
  t^2 vs t^3:  -b1^2/2 = -b1^2/3  =>  b1^2(1/3-1/2)=0  =>  b1=0  =>  g=0, b0=0.
  Rigor check: for b1=1, t^2 forces g=-1/2 but t^3 forces g=-1/3 -- INCONSISTENT: True
=> for ac=g != 0 and b linear, E[e^{tP}]=1 is IMPOSSIBLE. Extends Hermite (const b) to linear b.
